html:ul.html:li:
                (An intermediate notion) \overline {U} is the unique extension of
                U to a functor st π is natural in a.
                We've essentially seen this already, if not literally.
                For any functor U', naturality in a requires the following square to hold for all g : A(a, b):





\usepackage {tikz-cd}
\usepackage {unicode-math} 
                    \begin {tikzcd}
                        A(FU'a, a) \ar [r, "g∘-"] & A(FU'a, b) \ar [d, "≀"', "π"] \\
                        X(U'a, U'a) \ar [r, "U'g∘-"]\ar [u, "≀"', "π⁻¹"] & X(U'a, U'b)
                    \end {tikzcd}




                Thus, ∀g. U'(g) = \overline {U}(g).
                Then, with \overline {U} a functor and π natural in a, the
                precursor gives us a unique \overline {F} st \overline {F}
                ⊣ \overline {U} uniquely.
